# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 6 of the Tutorial (Part 4)

[Bo2's Drill Exercise 6.4 (DC)]

e,2,0,2
r,1,2,1
l,1,0,1
c,1,0,1/8

analysis: dc
note: The is-the-textbook-wrong problem, over four entries. First interval in DC: il = 2 A and vc = 0.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-6-4-35.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 6.4 (TR, the book's 1 H)]

r,1,0,1
l,1,0,1,2
c,1,0,1/8,0

analysis: tr
note: Solve with the schematic's inductor and compare with the printed answer. This is the point of the problem: the schematic says 1 H and the answer disagrees with the printed one.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-6-4-35.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 6.4 (TR, 1/2 H instead)]

r,1,0,1
l,1,0,1/2,2
c,1,0,1/8,0

analysis: tr
note: The same TR run with the inductor at 1/2 H. With half a henry the answer matches, so the schematic is wrong and the previous owner's pencilled correction right.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-6-4-35.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 6.4 (FD, solving for the inductor)]

r,1,0,1
l,1,0,l,2
c,1,0,1/8,0

analysis: fd
note: Reverse-engineering the inductance: transform the book's answer with t2s, solve the s-domain vc against it.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-6-4-35.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
solve_equations: -16/(s+4)^2 = vc
solve_unknowns: l


