[Bo2's Drill Exercise 4.5 (Expert)]

e,1,0,a*u(t)
r,1,2,2
c,2,0,1,0

analysis: tr
note: Expert Mode in TR: the step value a is the unknown, and the known answer 1-e^(-t/2) = vc is the extra equation. Find vr, ic and the source's value, which is 1 V. Everything typed into Expert Mode in version 9 is read in the time domain, so the answer you know goes in as you would write it on paper.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-4-5-expert-45.png [383px]
unknowns: a
equations: 1-e^(-t/2) = vc
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 4.13 (Expert)]

e,1,0,vs*u(t)
r,1,2,1
c,2,0,1,0

analysis: tr
note: The same trick: vs is unknown and vr = e^(-t) is known. The source turns out to be 1 V.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-4-13-expert-46.png
unknowns: vs
equations: vr = e^(-t)
rounding: exact
